    "result_text": "The full build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: default `registrationDate` to the server's current date\n\nThe feature lives on `POST /api/owners`: when the request omits `registrationDate`, the server stamps it with today's date; a supplied date is preserved. It's returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}` in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` form.\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`, optional) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` is `allOf: [OwnerFields, \u2026]`, this field flows into both the request DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and the response DTO (`OwnerDto`), which are code-generated at build time. `format: date` maps to `java.time.LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `LocalDate registrationDate` field (`@Column(name = \"registration_date\", columnDefinition = \"DATE\")`) with getter/setter, mirroring how `Pet.birthDate` is handled.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 The build step now defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the mapped owner has none. MapStruct already carries a supplied date across by matching field name, so this only fills the empty case. This is the natural spot in the OfficeFloor pipeline (`require \u2192 uniqueTelephone \u2192 build \u2192 save \u2192 respond`).\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 Added a `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in all four schemas (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres). The test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in `schema.sql`.\n\n5. **`src/main/resources/db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 The hsqldb seed uses positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)`, so I appended a `NULL` for the new column to each of the 10 owner rows (the other DBs use explicit column lists and needed no change).\n\n**Tests:** Both `AcceptanceTest` cases pass \u2014 `coreDefaultsToToday` (omitted \u2192 today) and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` (`2020-06-15` preserved) \u2014 and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
